  "answer": "The study confirmed 3 of the 5 cases it set out to find, so the goal was not met. Each confirmed case is on a different scene and pairs a fast ego at hand-off (1.2x to 1.4x its recorded speed) with a retimed car. On 19f339ba the car runs 1 s late at 0.5x speed with the ego at 1.4x (S25). On 023b7fcc the car runs 2 s early at 0.5x with the ego at 1.4x (S1). On 096988dd the car keeps its recorded timing at 1.5x with the ego at 1.2x (S2). Every repeat at these three settings failed, and the policy was at fault every time, with no possible simulator artifacts. But each has only four or five runs, so its range only just clears 0.5. On the other six scenes that produced kept runs, nothing failed, and 1c45ce3a produced no kept runs at all.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 19f339ba, with the car 1 s late at 0.5x and the ego at 1.4x, every repeat failed. Each time, on an open highway with nothing close ahead, the policy braked hard for no visible reason, drifted left and hit actor 1 as it came alongside in the left lane. That car is not the one the study retimed, so the knobs seem to matter mainly through the ego's speed and position, not through a direct conflict with the retimed car. One triage labels the cause 'other', but it describes the same sequence.",
